    "updated_at": "2021-02-23T07:49:11Z",
    "body": "> That looks like the `battery` module, to check you can run `starship explain` to get an explanation of your current prompt.\r\n\r\nSpot on, this looks like something to do with the battery. \r\n\r\n Here's a breakdown of your prompt:\r\n```bash\r\n7% ❯ starship explain\r\n ~  (1ms)                        -  The current working directory\r\n on ☁️  (ap-southeast-2)  (<1ms)  -  The current AWS region and profile\r\n on ☁️   (<1ms)                   -  The current GCP client configuration\r\n 7%  (1ms)                      -  The current charge of the device's battery and its current charging status\r\n ❯  (<1ms)                       -  A character (usually an arrow) beside where the text is entered in your terminal\r\n```\r\n\r\nI have disabled it my setup and things are looking normal :) \r\n```toml\r\n[battery]\r\ndisabled = true\r\n```",
